WEBVTT

00:02.220 --> 00:04.040
A long, long time ago.

00:04.380 --> 00:06.280
About a hundred years ago.

00:07.280 --> 00:11.360
This? Why this is
the story of a little girl,

00:11.620 --> 00:14.060
who travelled beyond the Door of Destiny.

00:17.540 --> 00:18.340
- NAAJA
- Nadja,

00:18.900 --> 00:20.170
With your eyes

00:20.171 --> 00:21.439
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:21.440 --> 00:22.650
- Nadja,
- NAAJA

00:22.653 --> 00:23.780
What do you see?

00:23.781 --> 00:24.910
Nani ga mieru

00:25.110 --> 00:26.550
Shining in the far distance,

00:26.551 --> 00:27.990
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:28.120 --> 00:29.225
The door to the future,

00:29.226 --> 00:30.330
Mirai no tobira

00:31.220 --> 00:32.840
That's what I'm searching for

00:32.841 --> 00:34.460
Sagashite iru

00:34.660 --> 00:38.330
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:42.560 --> 00:44.440
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:44.441 --> 00:46.320
Minna egao de aetara

00:46.440 --> 00:49.690
- I'm sure there would be no more fighting
- Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:49.820 --> 00:51.425
It could be so much more fun

00:51.426 --> 00:53.030
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

00:53.110 --> 00:54.820
The world is wide, but it's still one

00:54.821 --> 00:56.530
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

00:56.950 --> 00:58.600
I can't see the end of the journey

00:58.601 --> 01:00.250
Tabi no owari wa mienai

01:00.290 --> 01:03.620
- God is the only one who could
possibly know - Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:03.750 --> 01:07.340
- To the people who, someday, I will meet
again - Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:07.343 --> 01:08.400
I will go waving

01:08.401 --> 01:09.460
Te wo furinagara

01:09.760 --> 01:13.075
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:13.076 --> 01:16.389
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:16.390 --> 01:17.745
But I won't look back

01:17.746 --> 01:19.100
Ushiro mukanai

01:19.350 --> 01:21.830
Until the day my dream comes true

01:21.831 --> 01:24.310
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:24.560 --> 01:26.270
Nadja, Your smile

01:26.271 --> 01:27.979
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:27.980 --> 01:29.650
Nadja, gives me courage

01:29.651 --> 01:31.320
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:31.530 --> 01:32.990
Under the blue sky,

01:32.991 --> 01:34.449
Aoi sora no shita de

01:34.450 --> 01:35.865
I will find the place

01:35.866 --> 01:37.280
Ashita no yukue

01:37.870 --> 01:39.685
where my future lies

01:39.686 --> 01:41.500
Mitsukeru kara

01:57.020 --> 01:59.360
The star-eyed knight...

02:06.400 --> 02:10.340
The Starry Night,
A Waltz Just for the Two

02:32.100 --> 02:35.100
I got to meet... the
star-eyed knight again...

02:37.040 --> 02:38.700
The star-eyed knight...

02:42.900 --> 02:45.280
Anna Petrova, I've been waiting for you.

02:45.540 --> 02:48.900
It has been a while, Lady Queensbury.

02:49.080 --> 02:50.640
Oh, Anna, really.

02:50.760 --> 02:53.080
Please, just call me Emma.

02:54.100 --> 02:54.580
Oh?

02:55.040 --> 02:58.540
She is our troupe's new
recruit, Nadja is her name.

02:58.620 --> 03:00.100
I-I... I'm Nadja.

03:00.160 --> 03:02.300
Pleased to meet you, Lady Queensbury.

03:02.720 --> 03:04.280
Pleased to meet you, Nadja.

03:04.540 --> 03:08.120
I'm a devoted fan to the
hats that Anna makes.

03:08.540 --> 03:10.720
This is the latest trend in Paris.

03:11.180 --> 03:13.920
My...! How beautiful!

03:14.080 --> 03:16.320
This is such fine craftsmanship...

03:17.180 --> 03:21.680
I'll be the envy of everyone
at the upcoming tea party.

03:22.980 --> 03:23.980
How beautiful...

03:24.380 --> 03:27.040
She must be what they call... a true lady.

03:28.480 --> 03:30.800
Speaking of which,
Anna, I have a favor to ask.

03:31.040 --> 03:32.480
What may that be?

03:32.580 --> 03:34.420
The hair ornaments
that I got the last time...

03:34.500 --> 03:37.040
can you modify them to match this dress?

03:37.140 --> 03:38.960
Ah, that is a simple matter!

03:39.180 --> 03:40.240
How wonderful!

03:40.280 --> 03:41.280
Nadja!

03:42.080 --> 03:43.080
Nadja?

03:43.620 --> 03:44.740
Uh... Y-Yes!

03:45.460 --> 03:47.260
Head back without me.

03:51.360 --> 03:53.300
I wonder if I can get back by myself...

04:09.500 --> 04:10.980
Amazing!

04:17.460 --> 04:19.740
Oh no, I'm not here to sightsee!

04:20.160 --> 04:21.460
I have to look for the exit.

04:22.140 --> 04:23.920
Dear lord, that was dangerous!

04:23.200 --> 04:24.259
Excuse me!

04:24.260 --> 04:26.040
We're very busy today.

04:26.540 --> 04:28.660
You'd better return to
your work immediately!

04:29.020 --> 04:30.980
Uh, no... I'm...

04:38.100 --> 04:41.180
Exit... exit...

04:49.200 --> 04:51.980
Ah, uhm, I was wondering
where the exit was...

04:56.100 --> 04:56.920
Uhm...

04:57.080 --> 04:57.700
Who is it?

04:57.710 --> 04:58.840
Uh, it's no one.

05:08.420 --> 05:09.980
Please, take my hand.

05:10.940 --> 05:12.340
There we go...

05:12.760 --> 05:16.040
You were really a great help. Thank you.

05:16.180 --> 05:18.560
Uhm, would you happen
to know where the exit is?

05:19.240 --> 05:21.120
This mansion is really large!

05:21.520 --> 05:22.520
It is, isn't it?

05:22.620 --> 05:25.180
I occasionally get lost too.

05:27.780 --> 05:31.680
I'm so sorry, but I do not
know where the servant's exit is.

05:35.360 --> 05:38.720
What do I do? I'm completely lost now...

05:41.240 --> 05:44.740
I hope I will be able to dance with
the Lord of the White Rose tonight.

05:45.220 --> 05:46.960
The Lord of the White Rose?

05:47.440 --> 05:48.920
He's wonderful... isn't he...

05:48.980 --> 05:50.100
But, I've heard that...

05:50.180 --> 05:52.420
he's not very good at dancing.

05:52.880 --> 05:54.100
I wonder if it's true that...

05:54.160 --> 05:56.920
the Lord of the White Rose can't dance?

06:05.960 --> 06:07.580
Ah, I'm sorry...

06:08.160 --> 06:09.160
I made a mistake...

06:13.360 --> 06:15.980
Please excuse us, my ladies...

06:16.240 --> 06:17.240
U-Uh... I-I...

06:18.430 --> 06:20.560
Ne vous montrez plus jamais
devant nos invités!

06:20.700 --> 06:21.160
N-No... I'm...

06:21.200 --> 06:22.200
Martha!

06:24.720 --> 06:25.720
Yes!

06:26.500 --> 06:28.140
They sure come by the barrel, don't they?

06:28.320 --> 06:30.680
Girls who don't know the proper
way to behave in a mansion.

06:30.940 --> 06:32.860
Temporary workers just like you.

06:33.980 --> 06:36.500
Are you watching? Cut them about this long.

06:36.620 --> 06:37.620
You understand?

06:38.920 --> 06:39.920
Yes...

06:40.780 --> 06:43.900
If you don't finish it by the time
the party starts, you won't be paid.

06:45.620 --> 06:48.600
Uhm, you work at this mansion, right?

06:49.900 --> 06:53.260
I may look young, but I'm
officially a Harcourt maid.

06:53.460 --> 06:55.120
Ever since grandma's generation.

06:57.120 --> 06:59.580
I know everything about this mansion.

07:00.160 --> 07:02.220
Then... umm... awhile ago...

07:02.280 --> 07:03.920
by the back entrance, the star-eyed...

07:04.280 --> 07:08.080
No, I mean I saw a blonde-haired
man on a white horse.

07:08.400 --> 07:10.180
Ah, Lord White Rose?

07:11.440 --> 07:12.440
Lord White Rose?

07:13.020 --> 07:15.100
He's the young lord of this Dukedom.

07:15.540 --> 07:17.260
"The Lord of the White Rose", right?

07:19.080 --> 07:21.260
I want to thank this person.

07:21.480 --> 07:22.600
What do you mean by "thank"?

07:23.020 --> 07:25.800
He saved me from a
really dangerous situation.

07:26.760 --> 07:27.760
That's why...

07:30.020 --> 07:31.480
The young lord of this place...

07:32.040 --> 07:34.360
is always offering charity...

07:34.940 --> 07:37.840
to the poor, the sickly,
and all sorts of other people.

07:38.600 --> 07:42.880
It may be special for you,
but to him, it's one out of many.

07:43.160 --> 07:44.620
He probably doesn't even remember.

07:46.080 --> 07:47.080
It can't be...

07:47.660 --> 07:49.080
That's not how it is!

07:51.500 --> 07:54.320
Well, I have to go, and you
should go to the kitchens.

07:58.400 --> 07:59.800
What's your name?

08:01.120 --> 08:02.120
It's Nadja.

08:02.300 --> 08:04.480
Nadja, you probably already know...

08:05.300 --> 08:07.340
In this country, nobles
will always be nobles...

08:07.860 --> 08:09.480
and maids will always be maids.

08:11.680 --> 08:12.680
Lord White Rose is...

08:13.140 --> 08:15.140
a person from a world apart from ours.

08:24.340 --> 08:25.540
A person from a world apart...

09:01.720 --> 09:03.220
Granny's late...

09:03.360 --> 09:04.980
It's always like this.

09:05.600 --> 09:08.480
I'm sure it's because Lady Emma
has asked her to do various things.

09:08.960 --> 09:10.800
Nadja. Nadja!

09:11.500 --> 09:12.960
Can you go and look?

09:13.400 --> 09:14.400
Master!

09:14.620 --> 09:16.140
She'll be back soon.

09:18.580 --> 09:19.700
I guess it is true...

09:20.120 --> 09:21.520
He's of a different world...

09:22.220 --> 09:24.780
From Applefield... from
the Dandelion Troupe...

09:25.420 --> 09:28.080
Completely different
from the worlds I know...

09:31.920 --> 09:32.920
Huh?

09:33.160 --> 09:35.400
It's started, hasn't it? The ball.

09:36.680 --> 09:37.840
Don't tell me Granny's...

09:38.320 --> 09:41.160
off dancing or something right now?

09:42.640 --> 09:44.700
Oh? H-Hey, Nadja!

09:46.420 --> 09:48.560
Ah... Nadja! Na-

10:04.640 --> 10:06.740
So this is... a ball?

10:08.380 --> 10:11.120
Like the one... mother
went to a long time ago...

10:12.160 --> 10:13.160
A ball...

10:46.680 --> 10:48.400
My lords and ladies.

10:48.880 --> 10:52.340
Tonight, you have
come to the charity ball...

10:52.620 --> 10:55.320
to support the St. Peter's Hospital...

10:55.580 --> 10:57.380
and I thank you for your attendance.

10:57.960 --> 11:01.380
Now, the true sponsor
of this event, my son...

11:02.200 --> 11:05.220
Francis Harcourt, would
like to address you all.

11:09.120 --> 11:11.280
That's... the star-eyed knight!

11:11.980 --> 11:13.800
Thanks to everyone's support,

11:14.240 --> 11:15.600
a lot of children,

11:15.920 --> 11:19.100
and many poverty-stricken
families will be helped.

11:19.760 --> 11:20.760
But at the same time,

11:20.940 --> 11:24.380
many regions that need
hospitals with adequate facilities...

11:24.620 --> 11:25.840
still remain.

11:26.140 --> 11:27.140
That is why,

11:31.060 --> 11:34.640
I'm counting on everyone's
spirit of goodness and charity.

11:39.360 --> 11:42.500
Back then... he was so close to me.

11:47.500 --> 11:49.920
Now... he's so far...

12:52.840 --> 12:54.040
Your Grace?

12:55.000 --> 12:58.760
My, my if it isn't the Countess
Karlova. How are you?

12:59.060 --> 13:01.500
It has been a while,
hasn't it? Duke Harcourt.

13:01.940 --> 13:03.180
You as well, Lord Francis.

13:03.540 --> 13:05.580
Thank you for coming.

13:05.760 --> 13:09.080
My, Lord Francis, you've
become more and more manly.

13:09.560 --> 13:10.940
Let me introduce you.

13:11.960 --> 13:13.620
This is my daughter, Nina.

13:14.120 --> 13:15.280
I'm Nina Karlova.

13:15.640 --> 13:19.480
Thank you for... i-inviting
us, tonight. I'm honored.

13:20.040 --> 13:21.640
I'm Francis Harcourt.

13:21.900 --> 13:24.200
It is I who am honored to
make your acquaintance.

13:25.640 --> 13:28.420
Today is Nina's debut at a ball.

13:28.440 --> 13:29.440
My, my, is that so?

13:29.620 --> 13:33.200
I thought that she must have
a dance with Lord Francis.

13:33.240 --> 13:34.240
I see.

13:34.360 --> 13:36.660
She's still a child, so I
wonder if she'll please him?

13:36.740 --> 13:39.580
Not at all, not at all. She
has inherited your beauty.

13:39.900 --> 13:41.020
Don't you think so, Francis?

13:42.640 --> 13:44.040
My apologies.

13:45.900 --> 13:46.900
I am not good...

13:47.700 --> 13:48.740
at dancing.

13:52.140 --> 13:53.140
Francis!

13:53.620 --> 13:55.480
Please excuse us.

13:55.980 --> 13:56.760
Oh, likewise.

13:56.960 --> 13:58.980
Please stay and enjoy the evening.

13:59.920 --> 14:00.520
Francis.

14:00.640 --> 14:01.680
I'm very sorry.

14:01.940 --> 14:05.220
I've told you time after time that
dancing is one of the duties of a noble.

14:05.360 --> 14:07.520
Please excuse me, I need some fresh air.

14:07.600 --> 14:10.300
Ah? Hey! Francis! Franci-...

14:11.800 --> 14:14.420
That child's dislike for
parties is a problem, isn't it?

14:15.080 --> 14:19.220
He makes it obvious that, "It's for the sake
of charity so I have no choice but to come."

14:19.740 --> 14:22.980
He always refuses, so
"Lord Francis cannot dance"...

14:23.320 --> 14:25.020
has become a rumour.

14:25.320 --> 14:27.020
He's just like his mother.

14:27.320 --> 14:28.780
Amelia was like that too.

14:29.520 --> 14:30.680
That's right.

14:32.120 --> 14:33.220
That Amelia...

14:33.780 --> 14:36.600
She loved music and to dance, but...

14:36.840 --> 14:38.400
she hated parties.

14:38.860 --> 14:40.800
She'd sneak out every time.

14:41.180 --> 14:43.280
And sigh in her rose garden.

14:57.360 --> 14:58.860
Understand, Francis?

14:59.460 --> 15:01.860
Dance is an enjoyable thing.

15:01.940 --> 15:04.440
See? One, two, three...

15:04.560 --> 15:06.600
One, two, three...

15:06.680 --> 15:10.500
Right, right, just like that, Francis.
One, two, three. One, two, three.

15:10.780 --> 15:12.640
One, two, three.

15:12.880 --> 15:13.880
One...

15:14.660 --> 15:16.140
Shall we continue? Now...

15:16.420 --> 15:22.740
One, two, three. One,
two, three. One, two, three...

16:09.820 --> 16:10.820
You...

16:15.720 --> 16:17.720
Why...? Why do you hide?

16:18.480 --> 16:20.000
I-I'm very sorry...!

16:20.160 --> 16:22.480
I don't know who you are, but...

16:22.940 --> 16:25.760
honestly, I'm not a guest at this party.

16:26.840 --> 16:27.880
Please don't worry...

16:28.620 --> 16:30.640
I'm not one of the guards.

16:31.160 --> 16:32.960
Eh? Uh, then...

16:33.200 --> 16:34.200
I'm...

16:34.460 --> 16:37.760
just the black sheep of the
herd, that got sick of all the parties

16:38.300 --> 16:40.180
where people do nothing
but flatter each other.

16:43.000 --> 16:45.120
Why... were you dancing here alone?

16:46.480 --> 16:47.480
That's because...

16:49.740 --> 16:53.360
the waltz was so grand,
I thought it would be fun...

16:53.860 --> 16:54.860
That's right, isn't it?

16:55.360 --> 16:57.300
"Dance is an enjoyable thing."

16:59.280 --> 17:00.800
That's what Mother always used to say.

17:01.320 --> 17:02.320
Your mother?

17:02.860 --> 17:04.860
She was as warm as spring sunshine.

17:05.520 --> 17:08.620
But, she passed away
when I was eight years old.

17:11.920 --> 17:13.800
Don't you... feel sad?

17:16.660 --> 17:18.380
I was sad when I was a child.

17:19.540 --> 17:22.640
But, Mother left me with a lot of memories.

17:23.920 --> 17:24.920
I see.

17:25.680 --> 17:26.880
What about your mother?

17:29.880 --> 17:30.880
I...

17:32.040 --> 17:33.940
don't remember my mother.

17:34.440 --> 17:36.940
I was raised in an orphanage
ever since I was a baby.

17:37.580 --> 17:38.580
I see...

17:38.880 --> 17:41.820
But, I had many brothers
and sisters at the orphanage...

17:42.200 --> 17:43.260
so I was fine.

17:43.900 --> 17:45.500
I see. I envy you.

17:46.340 --> 17:49.200
I've always thought that Mother was dead.

17:49.940 --> 17:54.340
But, I found out recently that
she might still be alive somewhere.

17:55.000 --> 17:57.420
I'm... probably going to find my mother.

17:58.120 --> 18:00.120
But, I don't know where she is just yet.

18:00.960 --> 18:02.100
I'm sure you'll find her.

18:02.860 --> 18:06.620
Once you find her, you and your mother
can make new memories together...

18:07.640 --> 18:09.840
for the ones you didn't
have when you were little.

18:10.900 --> 18:11.900
That and more.

18:15.260 --> 18:16.260
Thank goodness...

18:17.120 --> 18:19.400
A moment ago, I thought
I was going to be scolded.

18:19.680 --> 18:20.680
No way.

18:21.440 --> 18:23.060
It's the first time...

18:23.160 --> 18:24.700
I've been to such a splendid mansion.

18:25.240 --> 18:28.020
At first I was going "How
magnificent", "How pretty"...

18:28.080 --> 18:29.620
I was so excited, but...

18:31.100 --> 18:36.140
somehow, the more I stayed, the more
I thought, "This is a different world."

18:36.900 --> 18:37.900
That's not true at all.

18:38.060 --> 18:39.060
Eh?

18:39.620 --> 18:41.396
"Whether you are an
aristocrat, or a commoner..."

18:41.420 --> 18:44.300
"whatever your lineage,
your wealth, your education..."

18:44.700 --> 18:48.100
"it doesn't have anything
to do with a person's worth."

18:48.640 --> 18:49.580
"The most important thing is..."

18:49.660 --> 18:54.320
"how this person strives
to live each and every day."

18:56.920 --> 18:58.940
Mother taught me as much.

19:08.260 --> 19:09.360
What? What's wrong?

19:09.920 --> 19:11.620
There was a shooting star just now.

19:11.660 --> 19:12.660
Shooting star?

19:13.120 --> 19:14.680
I didn't make a wish...

19:15.560 --> 19:17.520
But, it's all right, isn't it?

19:19.080 --> 19:20.320
By striving to live...

19:20.860 --> 19:23.120
and doing my best, I know
for sure that every wish...

19:23.860 --> 19:25.300
can be granted. Isn't that right?

19:26.560 --> 19:27.560
Yes...

19:28.200 --> 19:29.200
I'm sure it is.

19:42.140 --> 19:43.520
The star-eyed knight?!

19:44.040 --> 19:46.480
Will you... dance with me?

20:36.240 --> 20:38.580
The Lord of the White Rose... is dancing...

20:38.900 --> 20:39.900
But who is...

20:40.560 --> 20:41.560
Nadja!

20:42.160 --> 20:44.700
I'm Francis Harcourt.

20:45.340 --> 20:46.340
What is your name?

20:46.920 --> 20:49.660
Nadja... Nadja Applefield.

20:51.180 --> 20:53.520
Thank you for that night.

20:54.520 --> 20:55.520
"That night"?

20:55.960 --> 20:58.420
Eh? Uh, because, umm...

20:58.820 --> 21:00.960
You saved me from a dangerous situation...

21:14.200 --> 21:16.280
Mmm! Tomorrow, we go to France!

21:16.620 --> 21:18.080
Wait for me, my treasure!

21:18.880 --> 21:20.240
Huh? Where's Nadja?

21:20.440 --> 21:21.440
Ah?

21:22.620 --> 21:24.220
But... why?

21:25.000 --> 21:26.760
Why doesn't the star-eyed knight...

21:27.160 --> 21:28.460
remember...

21:28.620 --> 21:29.800
about that time?

21:30.660 --> 21:31.160
Yo!

21:31.620 --> 21:33.840
You feeling sad? Leaving your homeland?

21:36.920 --> 21:37.920
Yes, I'm sad...

21:39.440 --> 21:40.440
But?

21:40.620 --> 21:42.780
Across this sea will be France

21:43.220 --> 21:44.220
and Europe!

21:44.680 --> 21:49.140
And after that... on and on is a
world that's ever so wide! Am I right?

21:49.300 --> 21:50.300
When I think that...

21:50.580 --> 21:51.700
I feel so excited!

21:52.100 --> 21:53.960
Is that right? You're excited, huh?

21:57.080 --> 21:58.460
Star-eyed knight...

21:59.440 --> 22:02.380
If that person's fate and
mine are intertwined...

22:02.940 --> 22:04.620
I'm sure, we'll meet again.

22:15.390 --> 22:17.015
Paris is sunnier than London

22:17.016 --> 22:18.640
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

22:18.760 --> 22:21.850
- Carmen likes paella more than pasta
- CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

22:22.270 --> 22:25.355
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:25.356 --> 22:28.440
SUPEEDO no jou kimagure yasan

22:29.400 --> 22:30.640
- Indeed
- Kitto

22:33.400 --> 22:35.820
- It's not use worrying about it
- Nayan datte MUDA yo

22:36.400 --> 22:37.965
Que sera sera, sera Sera

22:37.966 --> 22:39.530
KE SERA SERA SERA SERA

22:39.790 --> 22:42.145
Tomorrow's going to
be whatever it was meant

22:42.146 --> 22:44.500
Ashita nante itsumo naru you ni

22:44.580 --> 22:45.960
- To be, to be
- Naru naru

22:46.290 --> 22:48.795
The tree fog won

22:48.796 --> 22:51.300
Sekai KAERU tobi KONKUURU

22:51.760 --> 22:53.720
The world frog-jumping contest

22:53.721 --> 22:55.680
Yuushou shita yo AMAGAERU

22:58.890 --> 23:01.975
Under the kitten's paw

23:01.976 --> 23:05.060
Koneko chan no ashi no ura wa

23:05.480 --> 23:08.565
Is the scent of the sun, right?

23:08.566 --> 23:11.650
Otentou sama no nioi dane

23:14.490 --> 23:16.155
Paris is sunnier than London

23:16.156 --> 23:17.820
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

23:17.910 --> 23:20.910
- Carmen likes paella more than pasta
- CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

23:21.410 --> 23:24.600
It's not the time to hang around

23:24.601 --> 23:27.790
Michikusa shite iru baai ja nai ne

23:28.670 --> 23:30.920
Indeed, indeed

23:30.921 --> 23:33.170
Kitto kitto

23:41.480 --> 23:42.780
- Tomorrow's Nadja
- Tomorrow's Nadja

23:41.480 --> 23:42.780
Tomorrow's Nadja

23:43.080 --> 23:44.370
Bonjour, France!

23:44.780 --> 23:47.061
We've finall yarrived at the
long awaited capital, Paris.

23:47.440 --> 23:49.860
There, we met the American boy T.J.,

23:50.060 --> 23:52.680
who turns out to be that
reporter, Harvey's little brother.

23:53.350 --> 23:56.360
But for some reason, he keeps
quarreling with Kennosuke.

23:56.500 --> 23:58.360
Geez, behave already you two!

23:58.960 --> 24:01.850
Eh? Those two are going
to help me look for Mother?

24:02.880 --> 24:05.700
Tomorrow's Nadja. The Diary of the
Ball that Ties Mother and Daughter.

24:03.660 --> 24:06.216
Tomorrow's Nadja. The Diary of the
Ball that Ties Mother and Daughter.

24:06.240 --> 24:07.980
Now, the Door of Destiny opens.
